<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection"><a href="#S4.SS3" title="In 4 Multi-Token Steering ‣ Steering Language Models in Multi-Token Generation:A Case Study on Tense and Aspect" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">4.3 </span>Qualitative Behavior and Failure Modes</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection"><a href="#S4.SS4" title="In 4 Multi-Token Steering ‣ Steering Language Models in Multi-Token Generation:A Case Study on Tense and Aspect" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">4.4 </span>Exploring the Effect of Steering Location</span></a>
<ol class="ltx_toclist ltx_toclist_subsection">
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S4.SS4.SSS0.Px1" title="In 4.4 Exploring the Effect of Steering Location ‣ 4 Multi-Token Steering ‣ Steering Language Models in Multi-Token Generation:A Case Study on Tense and Aspect" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Generation-time steering is more effective.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S4.SS4.SSS0.Px2" title="In 4.4 Exploring the Effect of Steering Location ‣ 4 Multi-Token Steering ‣ Steering Language Models in Multi-Token Generation:A Case Study on Tense and Aspect" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Steering before the verb works best.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S4.SS4.SSS0.Px3" title="In 4.4 Exploring the Effect of Steering Location ‣ 4 Multi-Token Steering ‣ Steering Language Models in Multi-Token Generation:A Case Study on Tense and Aspect" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Target addition does not require source subtraction.</span></a></li>
</ol></li>
</ol></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_section"><a href="#S5" title="In Steering Language Models in Multi-Token Generation:A Case Study on Tense and Aspect" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">5 </span>Discussion and Conclusion</span></a>
<ol class="ltx_toclist ltx_toclist_section">
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S5.SS0.SSS0.Px1" title="In 5 Discussion and Conclusion ‣ Steering Language Models in Multi-Token Generation:A Case Study on Tense and Aspect" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Syntactic categories are represented orthogonally in latent space.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S5.SS0.SSS0.Px2" title="In 5 Discussion and Conclusion ‣ Steering Language Models in Multi-Token Generation:A Case Study on Tense and Aspect" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Steering works for causal verification but is not a perfect method for model control yet.</span></a></li>
</ol></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#Sx2.SS0.SSS0.Px1" title="In Limitations ‣ Steering Language Models in Multi-Token Generation:A Case Study on Tense and Aspect" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Temporal Expression in Language.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#Sx2.SS0.SSS0.Px2" title="In Limitations ‣ Steering Language Models in Multi-Token Generation:A Case Study on Tense and Aspect" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Scope of Steering Analysis.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_bibliography"><a href="#bib" title="In Steering Language Models in Multi-Token Generation:A Case Study on Tense and Aspect" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">References</span></a></li>
